MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The magnet wire felt useful because I could use it to wind coils on the ferrite toroid cores I previously bought.",
    "That wire connects with my breadboards, PCB supplies, and relay module purchases, which suggest an ongoing interest in building small electronic circuits."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Wood, drywall, and sheet-metal screws require specific fastening projects that I do not currently have; being workshop supplies does not make them useful for my electronics tinkering.",
    "The belt, tap wrench, and pneumatic chamfering machine assume particular repairs or equipment needs I have not shown. Copper scraps also lack a clear immediate use, and my caster purchase does not establish a need for vibration pads."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My purchases seem to have been treated as a broad interest in hardware and workshop supplies, overlooking what each item would actually help me do.",
    "The caster wheels seem to have encouraged assumptions about furniture or machinery projects beyond the specific need that purchase addressed."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "Several of my purchases fit together as supplies for small electronics projects; a concrete connection like wire for winding toroid coils matters more than a general workshop resemblance.",
    "I need a clear task and compatible specifications before buying specialized tools, replacement parts, or large packs of screws. Possible usefulness someday is not enough."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my hands-on interests but mostly missed the specific electronics tasks that make an item useful to me."
}
